487
00:29:51,331 --> 00:29:53,081
- ... and not the whole pack?
- No.

488
00:29:53,249 --> 00:29:57,961
Okay, uh, how much do I have left for gas
if I just don't get any diapers?

489
00:29:58,129 --> 00:30:00,005
- Nine twenty-seven.
- Okay, 9.27 on one.

490
00:30:00,173 --> 00:30:04,468
Hang on. Hang on a minute. Um, here.

491
00:30:04,636 --> 00:30:07,638
- Here's $5 for the diapers.
- Okay.

492
00:30:07,806 --> 00:30:10,766
Thank you so much. Thank you.
You're very nice.

493
00:30:10,934 --> 00:30:12,851
- You're a very nice lady.
- You're welcome.

494
00:30:13,019 --> 00:30:16,396
No, really. You're amazing.
You're very nice.

495
00:30:16,564 --> 00:30:19,817
Thank you so much. Thank you.

496
00:30:21,694 --> 00:30:23,779
You and me both.

497
00:30:28,493 --> 00:30:30,285
You can't do that here.

498
00:30:30,453 --> 00:30:32,538
You can't change him here.

499
00:30:32,705 --> 00:30:35,791
Right. Okay.

500
00:30:36,459 --> 00:30:38,168
Thank you.

501
00:30:40,088 --> 00:30:42,714
Bye-bye, nice lady. Say bye-bye.

502
00:30:42,882 --> 00:30:46,969
Bye-bye. Bye-bye, nice lady. Thank you.

503
00:30:52,600 --> 00:30:55,435
Order up.
- Two more fries and a BLT.

504
00:30:55,603 --> 00:30:57,771
Husband Gus came looking
for you this morning.

505
00:30:57,939 --> 00:31:00,107
- Thanks, I saw him.
- So he found you?

506
00:31:00,275 --> 00:31:02,234
Yup. And a Reuben, light kraut.

507
00:31:02,402 --> 00:31:05,529
So who was the guy you were beating
the shit out of yesterday?

508
00:31:05,697 --> 00:31:07,239
Old boyfriend.

509
00:31:07,407 --> 00:31:08,574
Did you sleep with him?

510
00:31:10,910 --> 00:31:14,413
Figured you must have
after you punched him in the face six times.

511
00:31:17,083 --> 00:31:20,127
Hey, uh, Jackie's getting out
of the hospital this afternoon.

512
00:31:20,295 --> 00:31:22,504
Already? You picking her up?

513
00:31:22,672 --> 00:31:24,131
No, her parole officer.

514
00:31:24,757 --> 00:31:27,009
What, why? You called her?

515
00:31:27,176 --> 00:31:30,888
It's part of the deal hiring her.
Gotta call the PO if she relapses.

516
00:31:31,723 --> 00:31:34,850
Fuck that. She's trying.
Give her another chance.

517
00:31:35,018 --> 00:31:37,269
She's had plenty.
I'm not gonna be enabling her.

518
00:31:37,437 --> 00:31:39,229
She violates parole, she goes back.

519
00:31:39,397 --> 00:31:41,899
Hey, girlfriend's here.

520
00:31:42,066 --> 00:31:43,191
Oh, shit.

521
00:31:43,359 --> 00:31:46,361
I thought that was your big tipper.
- Yeah, it's complicated.

522
00:31:46,529 --> 00:31:47,821
It always is with you.

523
00:31:49,365 --> 00:31:51,408
Order up.

524
00:31:56,789 --> 00:31:59,458
Coffee and a piece of peach pie
you won't eat?

525
00:31:59,626 --> 00:32:03,086
I think I'll leave the apple á la mode
untouched today.

526
00:32:05,506 --> 00:32:09,301
- Are you and Jimmy lovers?
- No. He's not my type.

527
00:32:09,469 --> 00:32:10,844
You're my type.

528
00:32:11,012 --> 00:32:14,765
- Heh. I picked up on that.
- Really? I'm usually pretty good at hiding it.

529
00:32:14,933 --> 00:32:18,018
- Why are you here?
- I need him to make a decision.

530
00:32:18,186 --> 00:32:20,687
If he stays,
I have to make other arrangements.

531
00:32:20,855 --> 00:32:23,857
- Other arrangements for what?
- Business.

532
00:32:24,984 --> 00:32:27,194
So is he gonna stay?

533
00:32:29,113 --> 00:32:31,323
I don't know.

534
00:32:32,033 --> 00:32:34,910
I don't know if he's gonna stay.

535
00:32:35,078 --> 00:32:37,329
What mother doesn't care if they're crying...

536
00:32:37,497 --> 00:32:39,957
or if they're getting a rash,
or not sleeping...

537
00:32:40,124 --> 00:32:43,460
or if we're giving enough eye contact?
Worrying if the house is safe?

538
00:32:43,628 --> 00:32:47,339
They can hang themselves on curtain strings.
Electrical outlets are a nightmare.

539
00:32:47,507 --> 00:32:51,510
Toilets? Toilets? Toilets.
Kids drown in toilets all the time.

540
00:32:51,678 --> 00:32:55,013
Close the lid. You gotta be on it all the time.

541
00:32:55,181 --> 00:32:58,558
I mean, what kind of person
doesn't worry about this shit?

542
00:32:58,726 --> 00:33:03,063
My wife, that's who. That's who doesn't
worry. Sleeps right through the night.

543
00:33:03,231 --> 00:33:06,942
What kind of mother can sleep
through her children crying, huh?

544
00:33:07,110 --> 00:33:09,569
What kind of person, Julie?

545
00:33:09,737 --> 00:33:11,154
What kind, huh?

546
00:33:11,322 --> 00:33:14,324
You know that me jerking you off
was a one-time thing, right?

547
00:33:30,842 --> 00:33:34,970
Carol, Svetlana's asking for you.
She only wants Mrs. Hewitt.

548
00:33:35,138 --> 00:33:38,473
- We'll come get you when it's time.
- Oh, okay.

549
00:34:29,734 --> 00:34:31,193
You need something?

550
00:34:31,360 --> 00:34:32,402
Hmm?

551
00:34:34,030 --> 00:34:37,032
Waiting can be very stressful.

552
00:34:37,200 --> 00:34:38,241
Yeah.

553
00:34:45,583 --> 00:34:47,834
One hundred for the mouth.

554
00:34:48,002 --> 00:34:51,463
Two hundred for the...

555
00:34:54,884 --> 00:34:56,176
Do you think we enough time?

556
00:34:56,344 --> 00:34:58,261
- I don't want to miss the birth...
- Yeah.

557
00:34:58,930 --> 00:35:02,724
Baby takes hours to come.

558
00:35:21,577 --> 00:35:24,079
Baby needs a new pair of shoes, right?

559
00:35:27,083 --> 00:35:29,501
Back in a flash with the cash.

560
00:35:43,808 --> 00:35:45,725
How's it going, guys?

561
00:35:46,811 --> 00:35:48,353
Let's take a walk.

562
00:36:05,454 --> 00:36:07,080
It's okay.

563
00:36:11,586 --> 00:36:15,338
Help.

564
00:36:16,966 --> 00:36:20,010
Anybody?
We need to find something filthy...

565
00:36:20,178 --> 00:36:22,179
and ripped to put on Liam.

566
00:36:22,346 --> 00:36:26,391
The food bank always give us extra stuff
if they think we're homeless.

567
00:36:26,559 --> 00:36:28,727
Help me. I can't get up. Help.

568
00:36:28,895 --> 00:36:31,938
I need help.
You been taking your meds?

569
00:36:32,106 --> 00:36:34,482
Have you been giving them to me?
Not my job.

570
00:36:34,650 --> 00:36:38,737
Your job. You don't care for your family,
can't even make sure Chuckie and me...

571
00:36:38,905 --> 00:36:42,407
have a roof over our heads,
but we're supposed to take care of you?

572
00:36:42,575 --> 00:36:45,118
Okay, hands up. Skin turn yellow?

573
00:36:45,286 --> 00:36:48,705
A bit, yeah.
Probably rejecting your liver.

574
00:36:48,873 --> 00:36:51,208
Okay, Chuckie, you finish getting dressed.

575
00:36:51,375 --> 00:36:53,335
Okay? Nothing nice.

576
00:36:54,003 --> 00:36:59,007
Maybe that shirt with the bloodstains on it
from when you tried skateboarding.

577
00:36:59,634 --> 00:37:02,260
Chuck-o, help your old pap, will you?

578
00:37:03,179 --> 00:37:07,098
And don't help your grandfather, Chuckie.
He doesn't care about us.

579
00:37:10,895 --> 00:37:13,897
Liam, get me the phone, huh, buddy?

580
00:37:14,065 --> 00:37:15,815
Fruit of my loin.

581
00:37:15,983 --> 00:37:18,652
Apple of your pappy's eye.
You too Liam.

582
00:37:18,819 --> 00:37:21,738
Don't help him.
Liam.

583
00:37:23,908 --> 00:37:25,283
Jesus.

584
00:37:32,792 --> 00:37:34,626
Little cocoa ingrate.

585
00:37:40,508 --> 00:37:42,133
Help.

586
00:38:11,372 --> 00:38:13,540
- That's him.
- Hey, what are you doing?

587
00:38:13,708 --> 00:38:17,711
This your car, sir? Sir, you can't leave
a baby alone in a locked car on a hot day.

588
00:38:17,878 --> 00:38:20,005
I saw him get into a car and just drive off.

589
00:38:20,172 --> 00:38:22,132
You scared him. What are you doing?

590
00:38:22,300 --> 00:38:25,093
Sir, we were concerned
for the safety of the child.

591
00:38:25,261 --> 00:38:26,303
You called the cops?

592
00:38:26,470 --> 00:38:29,723
I get into a car for one second,
and you call the cops?

593
00:38:29,890 --> 00:38:32,267
- Are you kidding me?
- She did the right thing, sir.

594
00:38:32,435 --> 00:38:34,102
Now, why don't you calm down?

595
00:38:34,270 --> 00:38:35,895
Calm down?
You're telling me to calm down?

596
00:38:36,063 --> 00:38:38,773
Trying to steal my baby.
Telling me to calm down.

597
00:38:38,941 --> 00:38:41,026
Are you on something, sir? Drugs?

598
00:38:41,193 --> 00:38:43,403
Drugs? Am I on fucking drugs?

599
00:38:43,571 --> 00:38:46,906
You're the one who's trying to steal my baby.
You're the baby thieves.

600
00:38:47,074 --> 00:38:50,160
You're the ones trying to take my baby.
What is wrong with you?

601
00:38:50,328 --> 00:38:52,162
Who sent you? Did Jesus send you?

602
00:38:53,456 --> 00:38:55,749
- Did Jesus send you?
- Nobody sent us.

603
00:38:55,916 --> 00:38:58,543
- We're just here to help, okay?
- Don't lie to me.

604
00:38:58,711 --> 00:39:01,212
Why did he send you?
Get the fuck away from me.

605
00:39:01,380 --> 00:39:03,131
Stay away.

606
00:39:04,633 --> 00:39:07,177
Stop. Stop.

607
00:39:13,851 --> 00:39:15,018
Come on.

608
00:39:19,273 --> 00:39:22,400
Help me. They want to steal my baby.
They're trying to steal him.

609
00:39:22,568 --> 00:39:24,361
They're Gabriel's demons.

610
00:39:24,528 --> 00:39:27,072
That's right. Please. Help.

611
00:39:27,239 --> 00:39:29,032
Help me, please. Please help me.

612
00:39:29,200 --> 00:39:31,201
Help me, help me, help me.

613
00:39:32,244 --> 00:39:35,080
No tests. No tests. No, no, no.

614
00:39:35,247 --> 00:39:38,375
- Hold on. Hold on.
- No. No tests. No tests. Get away!

615
00:39:38,542 --> 00:39:40,752
- Get away!
- Calm down.

616
00:39:40,920 --> 00:39:42,003
Please.

617
00:39:42,505 --> 00:39:45,507
Calm down.
- I'm sorry. I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

618
00:39:46,175 --> 00:39:48,802
Please. I'm so sorry.

619
00:40:08,322 --> 00:40:09,864
What the hell are you doing here?

620
00:40:10,032 --> 00:40:12,242
I was running an errand
down the block for work.

621
00:40:12,410 --> 00:40:14,661
Thought you might have heard from Ian.
No.

622
00:40:14,829 --> 00:40:17,580
- Beretta Px4 Storm.
- Don't touch it.

623
00:40:18,249 --> 00:40:21,668
- So nothing from Ian?
- What the fuck do you think?

624
00:40:22,253 --> 00:40:24,337
Saw it a couple of times
with my mom, Monica.

625
00:40:24,505 --> 00:40:26,089
Kind of scary, weird stuff.

626
00:40:26,257 --> 00:40:28,967
Climbed to the top of our roof
and thought she was a bird.

627
00:40:29,677 --> 00:40:33,680
- She jump?
- No. The firemen came, got her down.

628
00:40:43,524 --> 00:40:46,151
- Want a beer?
- Sure.

629
00:40:48,529 --> 00:40:50,530
Got any weed?
Heard you're working a corner.

630
00:40:50,698 --> 00:40:53,241
Smoking the product is bad business,
eats into profits.

631
00:40:53,409 --> 00:40:56,786
Good thinking, kid.
You might just make it out there.

632
00:40:56,954 --> 00:40:58,580
Not a white man's game anymore.

633
00:41:07,798 --> 00:41:09,632
Two points.

634
00:41:12,845 --> 00:41:17,015
Yeah.

635
00:41:17,600 --> 00:41:18,641
Okay.

636
00:41:18,809 --> 00:41:20,977
Cops got Ian and the baby.

637
00:41:21,937 --> 00:41:23,563
Where the fuck is Terre Haute?

638
00:41:27,151 --> 00:41:28,860
So how long are we gonna wait?

639
00:41:29,028 --> 00:41:31,905
- Little bit longer.
- Are you sure she still cares about you?

640
00:41:32,948 --> 00:41:34,532
Yes.

641
00:41:34,700 --> 00:41:36,826
- We gotta leave for Dubai soon.
- I know.

642
00:41:36,994 --> 00:41:39,537
- Very soon.
- I know. There she is.

643
00:41:42,458 --> 00:41:44,417
I've been calling you for hours.

644
00:41:44,585 --> 00:41:46,085
Tough day.

645
00:41:46,253 --> 00:41:47,921
Ian?

646
00:41:51,091 --> 00:41:54,677
- Look, we gotta talk.
- I'm not sure I'm up for it tonight.

647
00:42:03,854 --> 00:42:06,189
Fuck, my phone's dead.

648
00:42:09,109 --> 00:42:11,110
I don't know what to say.

649
00:42:12,488 --> 00:42:14,906
Then don't say anything.

650
00:42:17,826 --> 00:42:19,744
What are you looking for?

651
00:42:19,912 --> 00:42:23,998
My phone charger.
Somebody's always taking it. Fuck.

652
00:42:25,376 --> 00:42:28,628
- I'm sorry.
- Fucking Sammi, probably. Shit.

653
00:42:28,796 --> 00:42:30,880
No. I'm sorry for everything that's happened.

654
00:42:38,472 --> 00:42:40,139
That supposed to be enough?

655
00:42:41,267 --> 00:42:44,602
- I should have been here.
- Yeah. Yeah. You should have.

656
00:42:46,188 --> 00:42:48,856
- I thought about you every single day.
- Don't.

657
00:42:49,024 --> 00:42:51,276
- You left. You didn't come back.
- I know.

658
00:42:52,653 --> 00:42:53,903
I love you.

659
00:42:54,071 --> 00:42:56,489
Don't do that again.

660
00:42:56,657 --> 00:42:59,993
I love you. I love everything about you.

661
00:43:00,160 --> 00:43:04,581
- Please. What do you want from me?
- I am so, so sorry.

662
00:43:10,838 --> 00:43:16,884
I love you.

663
00:44:07,436 --> 00:44:09,062
Fuck.

664
00:44:10,189 --> 00:44:14,233
Stop. Stop. Jimmy, stop.

665
00:44:32,294 --> 00:44:34,587
Please go home.

666
00:44:38,425 --> 00:44:39,467
Go home.

667
00:45:02,032 --> 00:45:03,574
Fuck.

668
00:45:03,742 --> 00:45:06,285
- Fiona?
- I'm just getting her voice mail.

669
00:45:06,453 --> 00:45:09,747
- Want me to try texting her again?
- Can't hurt.

670
00:45:12,376 --> 00:45:15,503
- I'm sorry, I should have listened to you.
- Yeah, you should have.

671
00:45:16,880 --> 00:45:18,840
I didn't know things could get this bad.

672
00:45:19,007 --> 00:45:20,925
It can get worse...

673
00:45:22,177 --> 00:45:23,344
get much worse.

674
00:45:33,313 --> 00:45:35,231
Mr. Gallagher?

675
00:45:36,358 --> 00:45:37,692
How are you feeling, Frank?

676
00:45:37,860 --> 00:45:39,986
- I've felt better.
- I would hope so.

677
00:45:40,738 --> 00:45:44,198
We've started you on Prednisone
to decrease the inflammation in your liver.

678
00:45:44,366 --> 00:45:46,367
Also Lasix to bring down your fluid levels.

679
00:45:46,535 --> 00:45:48,578
You were quite jaundiced when you arrived.

680
00:45:48,746 --> 00:45:50,955
Have you been taking
your antirejection meds?

681
00:45:51,123 --> 00:45:55,084
My bitch of a new-found daughter
hasn't been giving them to me.

682
00:45:55,252 --> 00:45:58,129
Your daughter has been keeping
your medications away from you?

683
00:45:58,297 --> 00:46:00,757
No, but she was supposed
to make sure I take them.

684
00:46:00,924 --> 00:46:04,761
Mr. Gallagher, you are a 51-year-old man
with a new liver transplant.

685
00:46:04,928 --> 00:46:08,139
You should be able to take responsibility
for your own medications...

686
00:46:08,307 --> 00:46:11,267
unless you're mentally incapacitated.

687
00:46:11,435 --> 00:46:12,977
Are you mentally incapacitated?

688
00:46:14,438 --> 00:46:18,024
- Mentally incapacitated?
- Retarded. Are you retarded, Frank?

689
00:46:18,776 --> 00:46:21,778
- No.
- Then get your shit together.

690
00:46:26,533 --> 00:46:29,327
- Am I gonna lose the liver?
- No.

691
00:46:29,495 --> 00:46:33,623
But we ran a tox screen and blood-alcohol
level as part of your work-up on admittance.

692
00:46:33,791 --> 00:46:36,918
I was happily surprised to find
there was no alcohol in your system.

693
00:46:37,085 --> 00:46:38,377
- You're welcome.
- However...

694
00:46:38,545 --> 00:46:41,255
we did find traces of cocaine,
marijuana and opiates.

695
00:46:41,423 --> 00:46:44,300
If I were to hazard a guess,
my money would be on OxyContin.

696
00:46:44,468 --> 00:46:48,846
Great stuff. Guy who invented it
should be on the Nobel short list.

697
00:46:49,014 --> 00:46:52,558
This is no joke, Frank.
Somebody gave their life so you could live.

698
00:46:52,726 --> 00:46:56,687
Well, technically,
I think he was pretty much dead...

699
00:46:56,855 --> 00:46:59,524
before they started divvying up
the body parts.

700
00:47:00,692 --> 00:47:02,568
I'm loading you up on antibiotics...

701
00:47:02,736 --> 00:47:05,071
and a new round of antirejection meds...

702
00:47:05,239 --> 00:47:07,824
and I'll be sending you home
in a couple of hours.

703
00:47:07,991 --> 00:47:10,910
If you don't take care of this liver,
you're shit out of luck.

704
00:47:11,078 --> 00:47:12,620
Nobody's giving you another one.

705
00:47:30,013 --> 00:47:32,807
- You coming?
- I should probably stay in the car.

706
00:47:33,308 --> 00:47:36,853
- Why?
- I might have a pound of weed on me.

707
00:47:37,479 --> 00:47:39,313
- Christ, there's a pound?
- Give or take.

708
00:47:40,691 --> 00:47:44,610
All right, you can stay in the car. But we're
gonna talk about this later, all right?

709
00:47:51,743 --> 00:47:52,910
Hey, excuse me.

710
00:47:53,078 --> 00:47:55,788
I got a call about my brother being in here?
Ian Gallagher?

711
00:47:55,956 --> 00:47:58,082
Yeah, that's me. I was the arresting officer.

712
00:47:58,250 --> 00:48:00,585
Does your brother have a history
of mental illness?

713
00:48:00,752 --> 00:48:02,003
Yes.

714
00:48:02,170 --> 00:48:05,506
He was acting irrationally,
left a baby locked inside of a hot car...

715
00:48:05,674 --> 00:48:07,800
and ran away
when we tried to question him.

716
00:48:07,968 --> 00:48:10,678
- Is the baby okay?
- Yes, he's sleeping in back.

717
00:48:10,846 --> 00:48:13,723
- Is the baby your brother's baby?
- No, he's mine.

718
00:48:13,891 --> 00:48:15,600
You're the father?

719
00:48:15,767 --> 00:48:17,977
Who are you in relationship
to Mr. Gallagher?

720
00:48:18,145 --> 00:48:19,812
His partner.

721
00:48:20,397 --> 00:48:22,732
Lover. Family. You know?

722
00:48:23,984 --> 00:48:26,652
We took Mr. Gallagher to the ER.
They gave him a sedative.

723
00:48:26,820 --> 00:48:29,572
It seemed to calm him down,
but he's clearly a troubled kid.

724
00:48:29,740 --> 00:48:30,865
Is he under arrest?

725
00:48:31,033 --> 00:48:33,618
He'll face some charges,
but we're not gonna hold him.

726
